{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"5c53c07a1857e167207c8a6980675a856bd14e91de6a7017b3088d311bfa8fc6","digest":{"component_or_area":"MCP server container provisioning","key_entities":["REBAR_ROOT","MCP_CODE_DIR","REBAR_TRACKER_DIR","MCP_TICKETS_URL","/app/.git","/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code","review_plan","verify_completion","reconcile","review_code","attach_commits",".dockerignore","Dockerfile.mcp","_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","docker-compose.yml","provision_code","Gerrit change 2271"],"problem_keywords":["attested-source gate","git metadata","ref resolution","container deployment","MCP server"],"propositions":["review_plan, verify_completion, review_code, reconcile, and attach_commits all fail with ref-resolution errors on the deployed MCP server because /app contains no git metadata (.git directory)","the container image excludes .git via .dockerignore and ships /app as a plain source copy with only a text marker .deployed_ref, so REBAR_ROOT unset resolves the repo root to /app which cannot resolve refs like origin/main or HEAD","gates using source=local do run but produce unsigned verdicts that cannot satisfy close gates, leaving tasks stuck in_progress with unsigned attestation errors","a real code repository clone at /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code (provisioned via provision_code with --filter=blob:none --single-branch --branch main) with REBAR_ROOT pointing to it enables attested gates to resolve refs and sign verdicts","the tickets clone at REBAR_TRACKER_DIR must not be reused as the code root because they have different lifetimes and refspecs, and code provisioning must not be gated on MCP_TICKETS_PAT since the code repository answers anonymously","the fix introduces residual risk that config discovery now reads rebar.toml from the clone at container-start time rather than from the image at build time, but this is acceptable because both versions agree at boot and the alternative leaves all attested gates unusable"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787856118400635001,"uuid":"4cd5d881-3096-48f6-aed4-3fd698d012d3"}